From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exynos6694 <azsx6694@naver.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:57:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Joy-Con rumble written to each Joy-Con's own HID device

A split Joy-Con pair played both players' vibration faintly on one Joy-Con and none on the other. GameController offers a
Switch Joy-Con pair the localities "JoyCon (L)", "JoyCon (R)", All and Default (macOS 27.2), not GCHapticsLocalityLeftHandle /
RightHandle, so a split half asked for a handle fell back to the pair's default engine, which plays on one Joy-Con only; and
GameController's Joy-Con engines are weak even on the right locality.

The Mac controller layer already holds each Joy-Con's HID device (pad_joycon_mac.h, for the IMU). Its rumble route now writes
HD rumble there, as SDL's hidapi Switch driver does: output report 0x10 with the actuator's four bytes (joycon_rumble_bytes:
the high band's 9-bit frequency and amplitude, the low band's frequency and 9-bit amplitude, the reverse-engineered amplitude
curve, frequencies clamped to each band, the neutral 00 01 40 40 for silence). The left Joy-Con plays motor 0 and the right one
motor 1, whether the pair is one player or each half a player of its own; the native output's 40 ms refresh keeps it going.
The route object retains the devices it writes, so a pair that changes replaces the route before a removed half's device goes,
and the merged player's route is made again when its pair changes under it.

GameController's route (DM_JOYCON_SPLIT=0) also takes a handle by the controller's own name (handle_locality): a split half
gets its Joy-Con, and the pair as one player gets an engine per Joy-Con, merged onto All rather than Default when the server
has no advanced players.

Tests: t_pad_hid (rumble bytes), t_controllers_mac (pair, split, removed half: report 0x10 and the motor each Joy-Con plays),
t_haptics_apple (a split pair and the whole pair with the Joy-Con's locality names).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Split Joy-Con (Switch 1) pairs vibrated on one Joy-Con only through GameController; HD rumble over each Joy-Con's HID device plays each side
Issue: none yet (exynos6694/NX2Apple-muti feature/local-wireless)

